### Variables
@baseUrl = https://localhost:7001/api/InAppNotifications
@notificationId = {{createNotification.response.body.id}}
@userId = user123

### Create a new notification (POST)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "type": 0,
  "content": "Welcome to our platform! This is your first notification."
}

### Get all notifications (GET)
GET {{baseUrl}}

### Get notification by ID (GET)
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{notificationId}}

### Get notifications by User ID (GET)
GET {{baseUrl}}/user/{{userId}}

### Update notification (PUT)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/{{notificationId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": 1,
  "content": "Updated notification content - Tour has been cancelled.",
  "status": 2,
  "readAt": "2025-08-23T13:00:00.000Z"
}

### Mark notification as read by updating ReadAt (PUT)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/{{notificationId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": 0,
  "content": "Welcome to our platform! This notification has been read.",
  "status": 2,
  "readAt": "{{$datetime iso8601}}"
}

### Delete notification (DELETE)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/{{notificationId}}

### Test with multiple users - Create notification for another user
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "user456",
  "type": 2,
  "content": "Tour has been updated with new information."
}

### Get notifications for specific user
GET {{baseUrl}}/user/user456

### Notification Types Reference:
# 0 = TourCreated
# 1 = TourCancelled
# 2 = TourUpdated
# 3 = Welcome
# 4 = PasswordReset

### Status Reference:
# 0 = Pending
# 1 = Sent
# 2 = Read
# 3 = Failed